body:
Source: user scope decision (2026-10-07) on BI-PF-0418; the delivery lane's documented limitation.

The delivery lane lands in the item's repo working tree (checkout target + merge --no-ff). Since the worker
scope is now product_forge ONLY, that tree is the PF repo (ROOT) - the live session tree - so landing there
violates IS-PF-0036. Provide a DEDICATED integration tree the lane owns:
- a runner clone (checked out on develop) or a worktree on a branch not checked out elsewhere, e.g. `<repo>-runner/`;
- `core/delivery.deliver` performs the landing (rebase/merge/push) in the runner tree, never in ROOT;
- the item's feature worktree/branch live in the runner's worktree space.
This removes the limitation and makes product_forge delivery turnkey.

Descriptors: module:core/delivery.py; module:core/vcs.py;
test:test-framework/tests/pipeline/test_delivery_runner.py.
